  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 122 PM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nMoisture advection continues Friday with a component of remnant\nmoisture from what is now Tropical Storm Vance in the far eastern\nPacific. Friday is going to be a wet day, with the onset of\nnumerous/widespread showers and isolated thunderstorms Friday \nmorning. PoPs are high Friday, with continuation into Friday night\npossible pending the exact timing of a shortwave trough passage \nembedded in southwest flow aloft. Look for a break Saturday into \nSunday, before moisture advection ramps back up late Sunday in \nadvance of an approaching upper low traversing the Intermountain \nWest. Another wet period is setting up for Sunday night throug \nMonday, with possible continuation into Tuesday pending the track\nof the upper low ejecting out of the southern Rockies. There is \nnotable model spread from Monday onward, but a trend toward \ncooler, wet and windy conditions early next week is noteworthy.",
